{
  "format": "llm-kit.project-models/v1",
  "description": "Shared cases of the extras a tracked project file may not set. The file is repository content, so binding refuses, in a row's request_defaults.extras and in a request profile's extras, the keys add_dirs, scratch_dir, output_schema, any key that starts with __llm_kit_, and network with any value but the boolean false; portable validation still accepts them. EVERY implementation of this format must run this file against its binding stage (Python: validate_document; TypeScript: resolveRequest) and must fail when the file is missing or holds no case. Each case has a tracked input ('lines': join with LF and add one final LF) that passes portable validation, and a selection 'key'. 'expect' is {document} (binding accepts; the normalized tracked document, which portable validation returns too) or {error: {layer, code, path}} (binding refuses the whole file at the first problem: layer is always 'tracked', code 'invalid', path the key's path; the error message names the key, the last segment of the path). The whole file is checked, in this order: the catalog rows in order, then the requests profiles in code point order of their names (not the key order of the file); within one extras mapping, output_schema, then the __llm_kit_ keys in code point order, then add_dirs, scratch_dir and network. The call layer and the code that calls a backend may still set these keys; a case does not cover them. Compare JSON values; object key order does not count. The contract is docs/reference/llm-kit-formats.md, 'Request settings'.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "row-add-dirs",
      "note": "A row's request_defaults.extras holds add_dirs (any value): refused, naming the key.",
      "tracked": {
        "lines": [
          "version: 1",
          "catalog:",
          "  - id: a",
          "    label: A",
          "    endpoint: api",
          "    model: vendor/a",
          "    request_defaults:",
          "      extras: {\"add_dirs\": [\"/work/extra\"]}",
          "selections:",
          "  k: {model: a}"
        ]
      },
      "key": "k",
      "expect": {
        "error": {
          "layer": "tracked",
          "code": "invalid",
          "path": "catalog[0].request_defaults.extras.add_dirs"
        }
      }
